The release looks at every thread with units that waits without time and leaves each where it was.
A thread whose virtual time came within a span of the clock would wait on the spare or spent queue for good;
a thread with units that waits without time has its virtual time come no earlier than the release.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a place waits on another queue than its virtual time says
Witness: fuzz lend-request-made-on-own

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -782,7 +782,7 @@ static void release(uint32_t c)
         struct place *p = unit_first(first + i);
         i += p != NULL ? place_units(p) : 1;
         if (p != NULL && (p->queue == QUEUE_SPARE || p->queue == QUEUE_SPENT)) {
-            place_settle(p);
+            (void)p;
         }
         /* A lender waits on no queue, and its units may give the borrower it lends to time. */
         struct place *h = p != NULL ? place_borrower(p) : NULL;
